#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059473 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4cc58a6-ebb8-544d-93a1-de6cbd5b180e" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by a Scalar"}] :question/id #uuid "4391bd7a-560e-5b59-bf5c-b68ff235c05e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4380" :question/problem "Calculate $-2A$, if \n$A=\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t2 & -1 \\\n        \t4 & 7\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack.$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $-2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2A & =-2[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\cdot 2 & -2\\cdot (-1) \\\\ -2\\cdot 4 & -2\\cdot 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ -8 & -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059474 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2da3580a-6a1a-5e38-bcab-bd35f1ea5a6e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Value of a Scalar"}] :question/id #uuid "69ac9cdd-b27b-5b90-be25-02252df54e9e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4381" :question/problem "If $k {A} =\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t1 & 3 & 4 \\\n        \t6 & 0 & -2\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack,$\nwhere ${A} =\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t2 & 6 & 8 \\\n        \t12 & 0 & -4\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "To express $kA,$ we multiply each entry of $A$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 12 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2k & 6k & 8k \\\\ 12k & 0 & -4k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t2k & 6k & 8k \\\n        \t12k & 0 & -4k\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack\n=\n\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\\matrix {\n        \t1 & 3 & 4 \\\n        \t6 & 0 & -2\n    \t}\n    \t\\right\\rbrack\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the top-left elements, $2k$ and $1.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2k & =1 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059475 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6727fdd-a614-5ead-9273-08c0a7fec997" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Linear Combination of Two Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "1828e8ba-504d-5b20-b5fa-82005c7588f6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4382" :question/problem "Calculate $2 {A} + \\dfrac{1}{2} {B}$, where\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and ${B}=\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        0 & 2 \\\n        4 & 2\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack\n.$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $2$ and each entry of $B$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2},$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A+\\frac{1}{2}B & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0 & 10+1 \\\\ 2+2 & 4+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 11 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276525 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6727fdd-a614-5ead-9273-08c0a7fec997" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Linear Combination of Two Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f89f41e7-5df3-5966-a4c9-681e9c1e6e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276527} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9c98bb-5124-5f3e-a39f-160bcfe4c0c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276528} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1baedc-39a6-5840-a74f-8ae7a05b54fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276529} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd1464d-5169-56ee-b089-de2692783a9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & -9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276530} {:answer/id #uuid "88f1bb1c-60cd-559d-87d9-b5e38e550f93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88f1bb1c-60cd-559d-87d9-b5e38e550f93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276531} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fabf40a-2fe6-5901-89e9-e8b6a7b1fafc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fdadda69-6d6d-5588-b3cf-6b7f92547348" :question/math-academy-id "q-11531" :question/problem "Calculate $3F+\\frac{1}{2}G$, where\n$F=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$G=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $F$ by $3$ and each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{2},$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3F+\\frac{1}{2}G & =3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot 1 & 3\\cdot 3 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-2) & 3\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3+1 & 9+0 \\\\ -6+2 & 6+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4cc58a6-ebb8-544d-93a1-de6cbd5b180e" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "660e0c80-1971-56b6-9a4c-2c73850bf26e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276534} {:answer/id #uuid "4211a664-1707-5520-928f-97bd63a7bfcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276535} {:answer/id #uuid "72aff9bf-d703-5e79-a861-ffbe47597181" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276536} {:answer/id #uuid "8a2a197c-9b2b-5b7a-8003-6bc5c3201403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276537} {:answer/id #uuid "b913873d-fe92-55ae-8876-b34274889a51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "660e0c80-1971-56b6-9a4c-2c73850bf26e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276534} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ddd53bc-9386-5f55-8a52-4f0d2c8407bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47b125eb-b57a-5684-9e37-c5a36b7cc4f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-125885" :question/problem "Calculate $0W$, if \n$W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $W$ by $0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0W & =0[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot (-1) & 0\\cdot (-3) \\\\ 0\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot 0 & 0\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6727fdd-a614-5ead-9273-08c0a7fec997" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Linear Combination of Two Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd48b2b1-b6be-54e7-ac0f-1ddac5b183cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276541} {:answer/id #uuid "355b262b-280f-5ee0-acbc-e0302b55c89c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276542} {:answer/id #uuid "005184fc-42df-5b1d-a1b6-062df7483660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276543} {:answer/id #uuid "8a406038-a8ff-53cf-bf5f-f555eb7d64ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276544} {:answer/id #uuid "ed252afc-cc43-51e8-9663-97f738cd55cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed252afc-cc43-51e8-9663-97f738cd55cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276545} :answer-field/id #uuid "20bc00ca-e64a-53dd-b5d8-fc98d199c87f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4843b32b-ee79-5d02-8131-fc83f01ea977" :question/math-academy-id "q-126009" :question/problem "Calculate $-A+2B$, where\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $A$ by $-1$ and each entry of $B$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-A+2B & =(-1)[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot 3 & (-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 1 & (-1)\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 0 & 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+0 & -1+(-4) \\\\ -1+(-4) & 0+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4cc58a6-ebb8-544d-93a1-de6cbd5b180e" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a304b8ca-b438-5fdb-a89f-1d22a196d6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a304b8ca-b438-5fdb-a89f-